{"id":"ARCH-005","category":"architecture","criterion":"consistency","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/config/loader.py","line":122,"code_snippet":"merged = _deep_merge(load_system_defaults(root), load_project_config(root))","reasoning_trace":"The Python reader merges the System catalog under the project config; the bash readers (adversarial-review.sh, flatline-orchestrator.sh, loa-status.sh, run-preflight.sh) and the TS reader read only .loa.config.yaml. A headless.agy_opt_in: true in .claude/defaults/model-config.yaml would opt cheval in while every planner reads off.","finding":"Six readers of the opt-in disagree on the layer they read.","critique":"The System catalog is integrity-checked, so the divergence needs a System Zone write; still a correctness gap in the 'five readers agree' claim.","remediation":"Read only load_project_config(root) in agy_opt_in_enabled.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1068 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1068.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py","line":912,"code_snippet":"if explicit:\n        return explicit, \"caller\"","reasoning_trace":"resolve_effort allow-lists the catalog and extra rungs but returns the caller rung unvalidated, relying on argparse. The function is module-public and takes any object with an effort attribute; a programmatic caller bypasses the allow-list and the value reaches the HTTP body, the CLI argv and the MODELINV payload. From the security dissent DISS-C-002.","finding":"The caller rung of the effort chokepoint is not validated inside the chokepoint.","critique":"Defense-in-depth gap only; the CLI path is validated by argparse choices.","remediation":"Apply _valid_effort(explicit) and warn-once/ignore on mismatch.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-20 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-004","category":"security","criterion":"info_disclosure","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/claude_headless_adapter.py","line":131,"code_snippet":"prompt: Optional[str] = None,\n ...\n        *([] if prompt is None else [prompt]),","reasoning_trace":"cycle-126 moved the claude-headless prompt to stdin to close the /proc/<pid>/cmdline exposure. The new shared builder keeps an optional prompt parameter that puts the prompt back on argv when passed. Both callers pass None (adapter :280, probe _cli_command). From the security dissent DISS-C-003.","finding":"build_headless_argv keeps an argv-prompt parameter that no caller uses, a regression surface for the exposure cycle-126 closed.","critique":"No current exposure; the test asserts short argv entries for the probe only.","remediation":"Drop the prompt parameter, or rename it to make the exposure explicit and add a test that the adapter never passes it.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-214 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/214.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-005","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/flatline-orchestrator.sh","line":533,"code_snippet":"mode=\"${LOA_HEADLESS_MODE:-$(read_config '.hounfour.headless.mode' 'prefer-api')}\"","reasoning_trace":"The opt-in itself has no env override, but the mode that decides whether a Google voice is agy-routed does (also config.ts:176). With LOA_HEADLESS_MODE=cli-only in the environment every Google voice becomes 'not planned' in flatline and Bridgebuilder, shrinking the cohort without a DEGRADED marker; the verdict is then computed over the remaining voices as a full cohort.","finding":"An environment variable can remove Google voices from the planned cohort while the PR's stated design is that nothing in the environment affects the agy gate.","critique":"Env is trusted in this framework and cheval honours the same variable; the removal is logged and carried in notPlanned / tertiary_status, so this is a design note rather than an exploit.","remediation":"Read the mode for the gate from the config only, or document that LOA_HEADLESS_MODE participates in the gate.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-15 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/15.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-003","category":"code_quality","criterion":"documentation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/audit/modelinv.py","line":498,"code_snippet":"# caller | catalog | none. Optional/additive.","reasoning_trace":"Compared the comments at modelinv.py:498 and cheval.py:2834 with the resolver (:921-926) and both schemas (model-invoke-complete.payload.schema.json:755-762), which have four values including extra.","finding":"Two comments say effort_source has three values; the code and schemas have four.","critique":"Stale comments mislead readers of the audit payload.","remediation":"Fix both comments to caller | catalog | extra | none.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1116 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1116.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-004","category":"code_quality","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py","line":914,"code_snippet":"if \"default_effort\" in params:\n        value = _valid_effort(params[\"default_effort\"])","reasoning_trace":"'default_effort' in params is true for an explicit null, so _valid_effort(None) logs 'None is not one of low, …' once per process. The extra rung lower-cases and strips (:924) while the catalog rung is verbatim.","finding":"An explicit default_effort: null warns, and the two rungs normalise differently.","critique":"Natural spelling for 'no default' produces a warning.","remediation":"Treat None as absent; the strict casing on the catalog rung can stay (matches the schema enum).","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-20 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html"]}
{"id":"DEVOPS-002","category":"devops","criterion":"reproducibility","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/defaults/model-config.yaml","line":495,"code_snippet":"# cycle-127 FR-3: bound measured 2026-10-07 by tools/ceiling-probe-live.py --transport claude-headless (Bedrock, global.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5); see ceiling_calibration.reprobe_trigger.","reasoning_trace":"The second commit's writer emits a clamp note (ceiling-probe-live.py:465: '; written clamped to 936000 (I2: …) from the measured 972887') when written < measured; the hand-written provenance line lacks it, so re-running the writer rewrites line 495.","finding":"The catalog provenance comment is not what the writer produces for this entry.","critique":"Minor drift between tool output and committed text.","remediation":"Run the writer once more on the head catalog or accept the drift knowingly.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1059 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1059.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-005","category":"code_quality","criterion":"usability","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/loa-status.sh","line":805,"code_snippet":"[[ \"$1\" == \"google\" ]] && ! _agy_opted_in && echo \"$_AGY_OPT_IN_NOTE\" || echo \"\"","reasoning_trace":"_provider_hop_note prints the opt-in note whenever the opt-in is off, regardless of command -v agy; after opting in, a host without agy shows 'hop -'.","finding":"The status surface shows 'agy: opt-in (disabled; …)' on hosts without the agy binary, implying that opting in would yield a hop.","critique":"Misleading operator hint.","remediation":"Check command -v agy before printing the note, or append 'not installed'.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1053 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1053.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-006","category":"code_quality","criterion":"usability","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/run-preflight.sh","line":204,"code_snippet":"p3_detail=\"no usable voice for ${p3_fail_stages% }: no credential present and no CLI hop on PATH\"","reasoning_trace":"When a stage's only voice is a gated agy hop, the FAIL detail says 'no credential present and no CLI hop on PATH' while the real cause is appended at :208 as 'not planned: …'. Pinned as written by PF-AGY.","finding":"The P3 FAIL reason text is wrong when the only voice is gated by the opt-in.","critique":"The operator is told to install a CLI that is already on PATH.","remediation":"Branch the detail text when p3_optin is non-empty.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1053 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1053.html"]}
{"id":"DEVOPS-003","category":"devops","criterion":"cost_control","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/tools/ceiling-probe-live.py","line":740,"code_snippet":"return hi          # the top was sent blind and missed: re-anchor it in measured tokens, once","reasoning_trace":"When the blind first step is a size rejection whose parsed count is more than tol from hi, next_target returns hi again (now scaled), which is almost always rejected again; the worst-case step is charged twice before the bisection starts.","finding":"Re-anchoring the top after a parsed size rejection spends a second top-size attempt.","critique":"Wasted spend at the catalog price for the largest step.","remediation":"Skip the re-anchor when the first sample is a rejection.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-400 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/400.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-007","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py","line":938,"code_snippet":"from loa_cheval.providers.anthropic_adapter import _effort_for_model","reasoning_trace":"_effort_on_wire lazily imports a private adapter symbol and is evaluated inside the _emit_modelinv(...) argument list at :2838 after spend. The emit is fail-soft (try at :2814, except Exception at :2873), so a mapping failure loses the MODELINV record rather than the invoke.","finding":"Emit-time lazy import of a private symbol inside the audit emit.","critique":"A refactor of anthropic_adapter would silently drop audit records.","remediation":"Compute effort_effective before the emit and default to None on error.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-755 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/755.html"]}
